    feat(landlock): kernel-enforced filesystem isolation tier (TJ-GAP-082)
    
    A Landlock tier for hosts where unprivileged user namespaces are degraded
    (e.g. AppArmor denying setuid/setgroups inside userns — this host): reads
    of credential surfaces (~/.ssh, ~/.config/terminal-jail, ~/.hermes, other
    users' home trees) and writes outside the workdir + temp dirs + ~/.cache +
    /dev are denied BY THE KERNEL, surviving exec. No user namespace and no
    privileges required; composes with (never replaces) the unshare/bwrap
    path, and is skipped where the uid mapping already isolates (mapped
    launch).
    
    - scripts/landlock-capability-probe.py: always-exit-0 classifier (FULL/
      DEGRADED/UNKNOWN + cause + remediation) reporting the max Landlock ABI
      (landlock_create_ruleset + LANDLOCK_CREATE_RULESET_VERSION), ruleset
      creation, restrict_self, and — preflight-the-property (TJ-DF-015) — a
      mode-600 read under the applied zero-grant domain returning EACCES.
      Machine-readable --json mode. Measured here: FULL, ABI 8.
    - plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/landlock.py: ctypes tier (no
      python-landlock dep, seccomp.py conventions): allowlist layout (denied
      = omission; the kernel rejects add_rule with allowed_access==0 —
      ENOMSG), workdir grant SUBDIVIDED around credential surfaces that sit
      inside it, HOME-as-workdir refused, file targets given only the
      file-relevant bits (EINVAL otherwise). apply() proves the EACCES
      property in a FORKED child BEFORE restricting the caller (never a
      half-applied state); sandbox_prefix() decides WITHOUT enforcing (a
      fork-isolated capability probe — the engine process must stay
      unrestricted for its own RuleLoader) and emits a
      "python3 <loader> -- " tail only when the loader is reachable by the
      launch's payload uid (0700/0750-home shape detected and degraded
      loudly). TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK=0 disables (silent when deliberate;
      one loud warning naming the cause otherwise).
    - decider.py: composes the tier through landlock_sandbox_prefix() into
      the wrap payload — single-sourced, exactly how unshare_prefix() is
      consumed. Without the tier, wraps are byte-identical to before.
    - standalone/landlock-loader.py: pre-exec loader (apply + exec, shell
      exec-failure contract preserved: 127/126); wired into the wrapper's
      bwrap arm, unshare arm and auto-sandbox rewrite dispatch with a
      readability preflight under the exact launch flags; install.sh ships
      it to the lib dir.
    - plugin/test_landlock.py: 31 tests — probe subprocess/JSON/verdict
      contract, kernel-level EACCES enforcement in a forked child,
      graceful absence (env knob + mocked ABI 0 stub via the probe re-entry)
      with the one-warning contract, layout/split unit tests, wiring and
      single-sourcing pins. Host-conditional cells SKIP with
      HOST-DEGRADED-LANDLOCK, never silently pass.
    - Existing backend/proc/modify/rule-pack suites pin their contracts with
      TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK=0 (the tier's launch shapes are owned by
      test_landlock.py).
    - docs: README capability-matrix pointer + probe row;
      docs/backend-parity.md known-limit (a0) describing the tier.
    
    ch:trace row=TJ-GAP-082 evidence=probe FULL/abi8/enforcement-denied (scripts/landlock-capability-probe.py + --json); EACCES demo: tiered payload secret-read-rc=1 ssh-read-rc=1 home-write-rc=2 tmp-write-OK vs host-side HOST-READ-OK; suite 1574+6skipped(before) -> 1604 passed+7skipped(after, +31 tests); uvx ruff check . = All checks passed
    
